n Row 6 (H6, I6, J6). By playing at K6, Black forms a "Live 4" (H6, I6, J6, K6) which has two valid winning spots: G6 and L6. \n- If White blocks at L6, Black plays G6 to form a 5-in-a-row (G6-H6-I6-J6-K6).\n- If White blocks at G6, Black plays L6 to form a 5-in-a-row (H6-I6-J6-K6-L6).\nSince White cannot block both ends simultaneously, K6 guarantees a win for Black. The alternative move at G6 would only form a "Rush 4" (blocked on the left by F6), allowing White to defend by blocking at K6. Thus, K6 is the optimal winning move.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "K", "row": 6}'}
